From aca41e8ef42f2618f64ac318acc74dbaf5554bad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:28:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-9pqp-7h25-4f32 (CVE-2024-8925): multipart boundary
 longer than the read buffer

A multipart/form-data boundary longer than the parser's read buffer was
parsed wrongly, so form fields and uploads could be split or merged in
ways the sender did not intend. Boundaries are now limited to what the
parser handles correctly (FILLUNIT - 4 bytes, more than the 70 that
RFC 1521 allows). With a longer one the body is not parsed and a
"Boundary too large" warning is logged.

Backport of php-src 19b49258d0 (Arnaud Le Blanc) with its follow-ups
c70e256308 (skip the test on Windows) and Remi Collet's 7.x test
adaptation; same change as Sury's 7.4 patches 0085, 0089 and 0092.

