From 46465c0608857e225758fdfdb022d1177cfd27c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:28:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix GHSA-cj93-vc83-wgqv (CVE-2025-14181): SoapClient chunked
 response length overflow

SoapClient kept the size of a chunked response in an int, so a server
sending 2 GB or more overflowed it and the client wrote past its buffer.
Sizes are now size_t with overflow checks and safe (re)allocation; the
redirect Location path allocation is overflow-checked too.

Backport of php-src b11bd1d939 (Nora Dossche, Jakub Zelenka) with the
test rework 3aedde06bc (Jakub Zelenka) and Sury's SKIPIF fix for the
test; same change as Sury's 7.4 patches 0154, 0158 and 0165.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
